===Verb===
{{en-verb|+|++|reran|rerun}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[run]] again; to [[repeat]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-06|author=N. R. Kleinfield|title=The Girls Who Haven’t Come Home|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/07/07/nyregion/the-girls-who-havent-come-home.html|passage=Ms. Hill has '''rerun''' those questions in her mind. “If the girls told me they want to stay where they are, I would have to leave them,” she said.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[broadcast]] (a [[television program]] etc.) again.
#: {{syn|en|reair}}
#: {{ux|en|They're still '''rerunning''' ''{{w|The Flintstones}}'' on this channel.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2008-09-08|author=w:Jon Pareles|title=At the MTV Video Music Awards, a Big Draw, a Punch Line and, Now, a Winner|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2008/09/08/arts/television/08mtv.html|passage=Earlier Sunday, MTV ran and '''reran''' a compilation of Ms. Spears’s previous appearances on the show, including her high-school hottie debut in 1999 and her on-the-lips kiss with Madonna in 2003, glossing over her lethargic dance number last year.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be [[broadcast]] again.
#: {{syn|en|reair}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-04-28|author=Caroline Framke|title=Beyoncé's Lemonade is on iTunes and Amazon — but will only stream on Tidal and Pandora|journal={{w|Vox (website)|Vox}}|url=https://www.vox.com/2016/4/25/11503988/beyonce-lemonade-how-to-watch-online|passage=Everyone is talking about ''{{w|Beyoncé: Lemonade|Lemonade}}'', {{w|Beyoncé}}'s new visual album that immediately became a sensation when it debuted on HBO on Saturday night. For those who missed it (and those without a loved one's {{w|HBO Go}} password), ''Lemonade'' even '''reran''' just before the ''{{w|Game of Thrones}}''<nowiki>'</nowiki> highly anticipated season six premiere on April 24.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[run]] (a [[race]] or other [[contest]]) again.
#: {{ux|en|'''rerun''' the election}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-08-18|author=Jeré Longman|title=U.S. Women Drop Baton, but Advance After a Second Chance|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/19/sports/olympics/relay-usa-women-drop-baton.html|passage=Thursday night, running in Lane 2 on an otherwise empty eight-lane track, at a half-empty Olympic Stadium, the United States women’s 4x100-meter relay team '''reran''' a qualifying round all by itself.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[run]] (a [[computer program]]) again.
#: {{ux|en|Restart the computer and '''rerun''' the installation.}}

